# The home server's schedule. Install it with:  sh ops/install.sh  (it keeps every other line)
# Stop everything with:  touch builder/state/STOP     Start again with:  rm builder/state/STOP
# The crawler reads sources into the store every hour; the publisher builds and pushes the
# site from the store every three hours. Each has its own lock, so a slow run is skipped
# rather than piled on top of the last one. The scripts are run through sh, because a
# checkout does not always keep the executable bit.
7 * * * *    cd $HOME/argus-web && /usr/bin/flock -n builder/state/crawl.lock   /bin/sh ops/server-crawl.sh    >> builder/state/crawl.log 2>&1
23 */3 * * * cd $HOME/argus-web && /usr/bin/flock -n builder/state/publish.lock /bin/sh ops/server-refresh.sh  >> builder/state/publish.log 2>&1
